  "description": "Send email through Resend's REST API without its SDK: one send contract (from, to, reply-to, subject, text and HTML bodies, headers, an idempotency key), a result that is sent with Resend's id or failed with a reason (auth, rate limited with the wait, rejected with Resend's message, transient), the RFC 8058 one-click unsubscribe headers, and Resend's delivery webhooks verified (Svix signatures, the Standard Webhooks scheme) and read into a small record. Expected failures never throw; the API key never reaches a log or a message. Templates, address books, suppression and preferences stay with the host.",
